      "revision": "e89a895a27a6634bded08f93c886b1a70bb15d63",
      "local_path": "dev-docs/performance/harness-perf-benchmark/README.md",
      "published_at": "2026-09-28T03:06:43Z",
      "date_kind": "source revision time; run dates are in each measurement",
      "method": "Process-tree RSS and sampled process-tree CPU. CPU uses 100 percent for one full core. Three serial runs per harness; the table uses the run with median end-to-end duration. macOS proc_pid_rusage at 100 ms, except the ccode Linux procfs batch at 10 ms.",
      "limitations": [
        "The runs use several batches and machines. CPU mean and peak describe sampled process-tree CPU; short-lived tools can escape these samples. Their separate child-CPU counters contribute to the upstream integrated score, which is not shown here.",
        "The author supplies a combined CPU/memory score, but this dataset does not use that score as a cross-machine comparison.",
        "The report gives one median run, not a median and variation for each individual resource metric."
      ],
      "method_urls": [
        "https://github.com/KonghaYao/harness-perf-benchmark/blob/e89a895a27a6634bded08f93c886b1a70bb15d63/scripts/perf/sampler.ts",
