      "published_at": "2026-10-22T03:33:44Z",
      "date_kind": "source revision time; benchmark run date is not reported",
      "method": "Linux process-tree proportional set size (PSS) after real model turns. The linked script defaults to five turns and session counts 1, 5, 10 and 20; the README does not state the exact invocation for its table. jcode and OpenCode each use one daemon for their sessions; other tools launch one process per session.",
      "limitations": [
        "The README omits tested versions, run dates, machine configuration and variation. Do not treat the linked script defaults as confirmed run settings.",
        "Model calls are real and use different providers or models in the default script. Context content and tool output are not fixed by a common recorded response stream.",
        "The README values changed from the earlier saved jcode claim of 32.9 MB first session and about 6.4 MB additional. This source reports 71.3 MB and about 3.3 MB. The earlier report is preserved."
      ],
      "method_urls": [
        "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/28d51019f7fdd30bbde69d40c87d59536314bd46/scripts/bench_headless_memory.py",
        "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/28d51019f7fdd30bbde69d40c87d59536314bd46/scripts/bench_memory_cli.py"
      ]
    }
